@startuml 4-menu-and-pricing
!include style.iuml
title 4. Menu, combos and pricing

class Menu MENU {
  - items: List<MenuItem>
  + {static} standard(): Menu
  + {static} withCombos(): Menu
  + add(item: MenuItem): void
  + get(index: int): MenuItem
  + size(): int
}

class MenuItem MENU {
  - name: String
  - priceCents: int
  - prepUnits: int
  + getName(): String
  + getPriceCents(): int
  + getPrepUnits(): int
}

class ComboMeal MENU {
  - {static} COMBO_PRICE_PERCENT: int = 90
  - first: MenuItem [1]
  - second: MenuItem [1]
  + ComboMeal(first: MenuItem, second: MenuItem)
}

class PriceCalculator MENU {
  - happyHour: HappyHour
  + priceFor(c: Customer, item: MenuItem, turn: int): int
}

class HappyHour MENU {
  + {static} DURATION: int = 2
  + {static} PRICE_PERCENT: int = 80
  + {static} RECOVERY: int = 15
  - activatedTurn: int
  + canActivate(): boolean
  + activate(turn: int): void
  + isActive(turn: int): boolean
  + turnsRemaining(turn: int): int
  + apply(cents: int, turn: int): int
}

class Money <<utility>> ENUMC {
  + {static} format(cents: int): String
  + {static} percentOf(cents: int, percent: int): int
}

class Customer DOMAIN {
  + billFor(item: MenuItem): int
}

Menu o-- "1..*" MenuItem : items
MenuItem <|-- ComboMeal
PriceCalculator --> "1" HappyHour : 2. apply()
PriceCalculator ..> Customer : 1. billFor()
ComboMeal ..> Money
HappyHour ..> Money

note right of ComboMeal
  <b>Inheritance + composition</b>
  A combo <i>is a</i> MenuItem (arrow) built <i>from</i> two
  existing MenuItems (fields first, second - composition):
  units = sum, price = 90% of the two (nearest cent).
  Order, Chef and pricing use it with no changes.

  Stage 3 menu (customers pick by position):
  | Salad | $9.00 | 1 |
  | Burger | $15.00 | 1 |
  | Pasta | $18.00 | 2 |
  | Salad + Burger | $21.60 | 2 |
  | Salad + Pasta | $24.30 | 3 |
  | Burger + Pasta | $29.70 | 3 |
end note

note bottom of PriceCalculator
  Bill when the order is taken:
  <b>customer discount first, then Happy Hour</b>
  VIP Burger in Happy Hour:
  $15.00 x 0.9 = $13.50, x 0.8 = <b>$10.80</b>
  All money is stored as integer cents.
end note
@enduml
